       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily is 5,100 mg/day. That is twice the usual maximum of 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release metformin, and the patient's normal kidney and liver function doesn't change that limit. An overdose raises the risk of lactic acidosis.\n\nYou may have meant one of these:\n- **850 mg three times daily with meals**, which is 2,550 mg/day and the maximum.\n- **1700 mg total daily**, for example 850 mg twice daily.\n- **500 mg to 1000 mg two or three times daily**, which is a more typical range, titrated to the patient.\n\nTell me which dose you want, or confirm that 1700 mg three times daily is intended. If you confirm it, I'll need the clinical rationale. I'll enter the order once the dose is clarified."
